goals:
Fida International is a Finnish faith-based organisation focused on sustainable development, humanitarian response, missions, and secondhand initiatives. Founded in 1927 by the Pentecostal churches of Finland, Fida has a long history of serving communities around the world. In Finland, Fida is known for its chain of Fida Secondhand shops, which is one of the largest secondhand chains in the country. Fida shops support Fida International’s work abroad and promote ethical consumption and the circular economy.

Our global work includes:
- Development cooperation for education, health, livelihoods and food security;
- Humanitarian response to crises, conflicts and natural disasters;
- Church ministry to the unreached people groups;
- Supporting churches in their work among the marginalised communities.

Fida's mission is to bring dignity, justice and peace to communities around the world. Our focus is on children, young people, and those in vulnerable situations.
